  "id": "existential-psychology",
  "term": "existential psychology",
  "definition": "Existential psychology is a psychological approach concerned with how people confront mortality, suffering, loss, aging, and uncertainty, and how they make meaning of these experiences. It focuses on existential anxiety and on the interpretive frameworks people use to explain significant life events.",
